    "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Number of Combinations of Objects Chosen From a Group Fewer Than Ten",
    "problem": "There were $9$ chess players who took part in a chess tournament. How many games were played in the tournament if each player faced every other player exactly once?",
    "worked_solution": "The number of combinations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{C}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $9$ players, so $n=9.$ We want to select $2$ of those players for each of the matches, so we have $r=2.$\n\nTherefore, the number of games is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{9}{C}_{2} & =\\frac{9!}{(9-2)!\\,2!} \\\\  & =\\frac{9!}{7!2!} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\cdot 8\\cdot \\cancel{7!}}{\\cancel{7!}\\cdot 2!} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\cdot 8}{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{72}{2} \\\\  & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
